changeSet.sql:
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_pipeline.pipeline_id IS
    'Synthetic identity of one pipeline RUN of one document (nexus-edjmu, pipeline-002-per-row-identity.xml). The unit both WAL tables key on; one row per (tenant_id, content_hash, collection, pdf_path). Returned by POST /v1/pipeline/create and accepted by every other /v1/pipeline route in place of content_hash.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_pipeline.keyed_by IS
    'Which create algorithm made this row: content_hash (a client older than pipeline-002, one row per hash, addressed by hash only) or document (identity="document" on /create, addressed by pipeline_id). Hash-only calls resolve to the newest content_hash row first so an old client is never hijacked onto a sibling document row. Dead weight once no released client predates the engine cut carrying pipeline-002.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_pages.pipeline_id IS
    'Owning run (nexus-edjmu): FK (tenant_id, pipeline_id) -> pdf_pipeline ON DELETE CASCADE. content_hash was dropped from this table in pipeline-002-2 so no hash-scoped WAL query can exist; derive it through the parent row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_chunks.pipeline_id IS
    'Owning run (nexus-edjmu): FK (tenant_id, pipeline_id) -> pdf_pipeline ON DELETE CASCADE. uploaded is a per-run fact: a second document sharing the bytes uploads its own copy of the same chunk text (RDR-181 skips the re-embed; the manifest is per document). content_hash was dropped from this table in pipeline-002-2.';

changeSet.rollback:
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_chunks.pipeline_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_pages.pipeline_id IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_pipeline.keyed_by IS NULL;
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.pdf_pipeline.pipeline_id IS NULL;
